Views

This directory contains all Twig templates used to render HTML pages for the application.

------------------------------
Responsibilities

- Define the presentation layer of the application.
- Render dynamic content passed from controllers.
- Include reusable components to avoid duplication.
- Handle markup, layout, and presentation logic only — no business logic or database access.

Views should never contain PHP logic for database operations or HTTP handling. Those responsibilities belong to controllers, services, or DAOs.

------------------------------
Structure

- Main templates: Each page typically has a Twig file named after its route, e.g., index.twig, portfolio.twig, contact.twig.
- Components: Shared partial templates (like headers, footers, navigation menus) live in a components/ subfolder. They are included in main templates using Twig {% include %} or {% embed %}.

-----------------------------
Directory Structure

- views/ – Root directory for all Twig view templates
    -> components/ – Reusable UI components shared across pages
        -> svgs/ – SVG icons stored as Twig partials
            -> arrowDown.twig – SVG icon for a downward arrow
            -> github.twig – SVG icon for GitHub logo
            -> linkedIn.twig – SVG icon for LinkedIn logo
            ->settings.twig – SVG icon representing settings or configuration
        -> base.twig – Base layout template (HTML skeleton, blocks, meta, etc.)
        -> footer.twig – Footer component used across pages
        -> githubLink.twig – Component for a GitHub profile or repository link
        -> header.twig – Header/navigation component
    -> contact.twig – Contact page template
    -> index.twig – Homepage template
    -> portfolio.twig – Portfolio or projects listing page
    -> status.twig – Status or system information page
    -> readme – Documentation or notes related to the views folder